### Disable Platform-Native Automerge

Source: https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/blob/main/docs/usage/key-concepts/automerge.md

Disable Renovate's default platform-native automerge by setting 'platformAutomerge' to false. This example also shows configuration for lock file maintenance.

```json
{
  "lockFileMaintenance": {
    "enabled": true,
    "automerge": true,
    "automergeType": "pr",
    "platformAutomerge": false
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Renovate for Automerge

Source: https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/blob/main/docs/usage/key-concepts/automerge.md

Set `automerge: true` in your Renovate configuration to allow automerging of updates. This example configures automerging for minor and patch updates.

```json
{
  "packageRules": [
    {
      "description": "Automerge non-major updates",
      "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
      "automerge": true
    }
  ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure packageRules to disable minimumReleaseAge for pinDigest

Source: https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/blob/main/docs/usage/key-concepts/minimum-release-age.md

Uses packageRules to scope a shorter or disabled minimumReleaseAge specifically to pinDigest updates.

```json
{
  "packageRules": [
    {
      "matchUpdateTypes": ["pinDigest"],
      "minimumReleaseAge": null
    }
  ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### packageRules validation: selectors, non-match fields required, matchUpdateTypes restrictions

Source: https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/blob/main/lib/config/validation.ts

Each `packageRules` entry must contain at least one match* selector and at least one non-match* field. Additionally, `matchUpdateTypes` cannot be combined with pre-lookup options like `allowedVersions`, `rangeStrategy`, or `registryUrls`.

```typescript
const selectors = [
  'matchFileNames', 'matchLanguages', 'matchCategories',
  'matchBaseBranches', 'matchManagers', 'matchDatasources',
  'matchDepTypes', 'matchDepNames', 'matchPackageNames',
  'matchCurrentValue', 'matchCurrentVersion', 'matchSourceUrls',
  'matchRegistryUrls', 'matchUpdateTypes', 'matchConfidence',
  'matchCurrentAge', 'matchRepositories', 'matchNewValue',
  'matchJsonata',
];
if (key === 'packageRules') {
  for (const [subIndex, packageRule] of val.entries()) {
    if (isObject(packageRule)) {
      const selectorLength = Object.keys(resolvedRule).filter(
        (ruleKey) => selectors.includes(ruleKey),
      ).length;
      if (!selectorLength) {
        errors.push({
          topic: 'Configuration Error',
          message: `${currentPath}[${subIndex}]: Each packageRule must contain at least one match* or exclude* selector.`,
        });
      }
      if (selectorLength === Object.keys(resolvedRule).length) {
        warnings.push({
          topic: 'Configuration Error',
          message: `${currentPath}[${subIndex}]: Each packageRule must contain at least one non-match* or non-exclude* field.`,
        });
      }
      const preLookupOptions = [
        'allowedVersions', 'extractVersion', 'followTag', 'ignoreDeps',
        'ignoreUnstable', 'rangeStrategy', 'registryUrls', 'respectLatest',
        'rollbackPrs', 'separateMajorMinor', 'separateMinorPatch',
        'separateMultipleMajor', 'separateMultipleMinor', 'versioning',
      ];
      if (isNonEmptyArray(resolvedRule.matchUpdateTypes)) {
        for (const option of preLookupOptions) {
          if (resolvedRule[option] !== undefined) {
            errors.push({
              topic: 'Configuration Error',
              message: `${currentPath}[${subIndex}]: packageRules cannot combine both matchUpdateTypes and ${option}.`,
            });
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Configuration Options > platformAutomerge

Source: https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/blob/main/docs/usage/configuration-options.md

Platform automerge allows Renovate to leverage native merge functionality on platforms like GitHub, GitLab, and Bitbucket. When enabled, it is critical to configure branch protection rules to require status checks, as the platform may otherwise merge PRs before tests complete or pass. If using required status checks for artifact updates, the statusCheckWhen.artifactError setting must be configured to always to ensure the check status is correctly reported.

